course: dictionary
lesson: 3035
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word early has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «The bus came early.» Early here means before the usual time. Ask yourself: early compared with what?
explain: «It was early morning when the sun came up.» Here early means near the beginning of the day. «Children born early in the school year» uses the same idea: near the start of the year. Same word, different clue.
explain: Early can also mean long ago or first. In «an early earthquake detector», early means it was made a long time ago, one of the first of its kind. Earlier means before something else, so when you see earlier, look for what it is being compared with.
fact: Early can be an adjective (an early bus) or an adverb (we arrived early).
fact: «Early» means before the usual or expected time, as in «The bus came early».
fact: «Early» can mean near the beginning of a day, a period or an event, as in «early morning».
fact: «Early» can mean happening long ago or first, as in early cars or an early earthquake detector.
fact: «Earlier» means before, and «at the earliest» means no sooner than a certain time.
exercise: «The bus came early.» What does early mean here? | Near the end of the day | *Before the usual time | Very loudly | Long ago
exercise: «In 2020 a Przewalski's horse foal called Kurt was cloned from cells frozen 40 years earlier.» What does earlier mean here? | Very quickly | *Further back in time, before the cloning | Later, after the cloning | Exactly on time
exercise: Which phrase means near the start of a day? | Very quiet | Late at night | *Early morning | Long ago
test: «He arrived 5 minutes early for the match.» What does 5 minutes early mean? | *5 minutes before the set time | 5 minutes of rain | 5 minutes long | 5 minutes after the start
test: «Athens and Iceland's Althing had assemblies much earlier.» What does earlier mean here? | Very quickly | *Before, so they came first in history | After, so they came last | At the same time
exam: «Children born early in the school year can be almost a year older than classmates.» Which meaning of early is used here? | *Near the beginning of a period | Before the usual time | Very quickly | Happening long ago or first
